Part of the group of the four main disciples of rNgog Blo ldan shes rab (ID:3786) exX0032026-09-0202-25-28 .</note></person><person xml:id="person3807"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bre shes rab 'bar</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འབྲེ་ཤེས་རབ་འབར</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bre chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'dre chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'dre shes rab 'bar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bri shes rab 'bar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shes rab bla ma</persName><birth notBefore="1040-01-01" notAfter="1100-12-31">after 1040 before 1100</birth><death notAfter="1200-12-31">before 1200</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2274</idno><idno type="APIS">3807</idno><note type="comment">Further holy places associated to him are: Ze thang, Grwa thang and rMog po ([647FFPZR]: 545, based on [Q3KCZX7B]: 38).&#13;
Remembered for thirteen distinguished objects (such as royal insignia and religious articles), which could be objects of his clan ([4LDAV8UH]: 95.).</note></person><person xml:id="person3809"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khyung rin chen grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཁྱུང་རིན་ཆེན་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">jo btsun</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">jo btsun khyung</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slang pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">glang pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">glang pha ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slang pha ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rin chen grags</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khyung</persName><birth notBefore="1000-01-01" notAfter="1083-12-31">after 1000 before 1083</birth><death notAfter="1170-12-31">before 1170</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P5746</idno><idno type="APIS">3809</idno><note type="comment">His dates can be approximated as 1070-1130.&#13;
&#13;
He is possibly the same person as Byang 'chad khyung (ID:6382), as [NA9AMDH6] states that Khyung rin chen grags held Byang 'chad (ID:4416) and taught Sa chen (ID:4205) there ([647FFPZR]: 543). [CJ75QQKN]: 339 (fol. 8a/170a1-3).&#13;
dMar ston's Zhib mo rdo rje ([RA3FK3BK]: 134 and 137), on the other hand, distinguish the two figures and places Sa chen's studies with Khyung at Nyang stod byang 'chad, and those with Khyung rin chen grags at Nyang stod.&#13;
&#13;
On the reference to Khyung as "slang pa/slang pha/slang pha ba" (understood as a regionalism for "glang pa/glang pha ba," see [WL39GVT5]: 940.</note></person><person xml:id="person3816"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ar byang chub ye shes</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཨར་བྱང་ཆུབ་ཡེ་ཤེས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shag kya'i dge slong byang chub ye shes</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shag kya'i dge slong byang ye</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">a ro byang chub ye shes</persName><birth notBefore="1054-01-01" notAfter="1056-12-31">after 1054 before 1056</birth><death notBefore="1134-01-01" notAfter="1194-12-31">after 1134 before 1194</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2552</idno><idno type="APIS">3816</idno><note type="comment">Dates according to [2V6H2FBU]: 24, n. 70 ("Since Ar was invited as a dge bshes to a monastery in 1076, it is hard to believe that he was not at least 20 years old, which would put his birth-date at least in 1056. The last trace of his existence is in 1144 when he took over the head of rgyal lha khang.").</note></person><person xml:id="person3820"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'dul 'dzin dkar mo</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འདུལ་འཛིན་དཀར་མོ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gzhon nu tshul khrims</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gzhon nu tshul 'khrims</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bsam yas pa 'dul kar</persName><birth notBefore="1069-01-01" notAfter="1159-12-31">after 1069 before 1159</birth><death notBefore="1129-01-01" notAfter="1249-12-31">after 1129 before 1249</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P0RK982</idno><idno type="APIS">3820</idno><note type="comment">[MGPRHX73]: 58, n. 24 cites an 18th century work that argues that "gzhon nu tshul khrims" is the real name of 'Dul 'dzin dkar mo (ID:3820) and "shes rab 'bum" that of his student dKar chung ring mo (ID:3821).</note></person><person xml:id="person3840"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dan bag pa smra ba'i seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">དན་བག་པ་སྨྲ་བའི་སེང་གེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'dan bag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dan 'bag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dan bag</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">smra ba'i seng ge dan 'bag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">smra ba'i seng+ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">smra seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma bkra shis</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dan 'bag pa dar seng</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dan phag pa dar ma seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dang 'bag smra ba'i seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">smra ba'i seng ge dar 'bag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsang pa dan phag</persName><birth notBefore="1050-01-01" notAfter="1159-12-31">after 1050 before 1159</birth><death notBefore="1140-01-01" notAfter="1230-12-31">after 1140 before 1230</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4747</idno><idno type="APIS">3840</idno><note type="comment">Part of the group of Phya pa (ID:3831)'s students referred to as the "Eight Mighty Lions."&#13;
Possibly identical with (ID:6217) ([4LWBNM7B]: 106).&#13;
Maybe the same person as the "Chos kyi grags pa" mentioned as lineage successor of gTsang nag pa (ID:3839) and predecessor of gNyal zhig (ID:3887) in Bu ston's lineage of the Pramāṇaviniścaya (ID:3774).</note></person><person xml:id="person3887"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyal zhig po 'jam pa'i rdo rje</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཉལ་ཞིག་པོ་འཇམ་པའི་རྡོ་རྗེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyal pa zhig po 'jam pa'i rdo rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dmyal zhig po 'jam pa'i rdo rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam pa'i rdo rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam dpal seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam gsar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shes rab blo gros</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mnyal zhig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">snyal zhig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dmyag zhig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">nyal zhig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyal pa zhig pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">yul dbus kyi slob dpon 'jam pa'i rdo rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dnyal pa zhig po</persName><birth notBefore="1130-01-01" notAfter="1200-12-31">after 1130 before 1200</birth><death notBefore="1200-01-01" notAfter="1275-12-31">after 1200 before 1275</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P8724</idno><idno type="APIS">3887</idno><note type="comment">Fl. late 12th to early 13th c. [MPRU5QUC] records the name of this abbot as "'Jam dpal seng ge."&#13;
